issue.body:
I'm using netty-all-4.0.23.
The OioEventLoopGroup execute a task used so lang a time (2000ms), I think it's maybe a bug in OioEventLoopGroup or SingleThreadEventExecutor.

```
        OioEventLoopGroup eventLoopGroup = new OioEventLoopGroup();

        Bootstrap b = new Bootstrap();
        Channel channel = b.group(eventLoopGroup)
                .channel(RxtxChannel.class)
                .option(ChannelOption.AUTO_READ, true)
                .handler(new ChannelInitializer<RxtxChannel>() {
                    @Override
                    public void initChannel(RxtxChannel ch) throws Exception {
                    }
                })
                .connect(new RxtxDeviceAddress("COM1")).sync().channel();

        log.debug("schedule");
        final long t = System.currentTimeMillis();
        channel.eventLoop().schedule(new Runnable() {
            @Override
            public void run() {
                log.debug("schedule executed, use time: {}ms", System.currentTimeMillis() - t);
            }
        }, 0, TimeUnit.MILLISECONDS);

        log.debug("execute");
        final long t1 = System.currentTimeMillis();
        channel.eventLoop().execute(new Runnable() {
            @Override
            public void run() {
                log.debug("runnable executed, use time: {}ms", System.currentTimeMillis() - t1);
            }
        });

        channel.close();
        eventLoopGroup.shutdownGracefully();
```
